# an inhabitant (world/bodies/inhabitant.obend, a body over RECORD): a thing that lives in a place and keeps
# its own hours there. Its rules on the tide and on the places it haunts are its own, placed as itself
# (`@<id>`) by the rule below when it is made or its maker arms it; they move it (presence, by the place's
# own `enter` and `leave`), and it leaves lines where it goes. A kind of it (`of: kind/inhabitant`) gives
# a character its voice, its verbs and what it does at which hour (its body's `haunting`).
of: record
form: <<END
name: text 1..64
haunts: object 1..128
tide: object 1..128
END
head: {name}
voice: one who lives here and keeps its own hours; what it does it has done before, and does again
about: lives in a place by its own hours: its own rules on the tide move it, and it leaves lines where it goes
text: rule haunts "places its own rules where it haunts, as itself, when it is made, armed or its haunt or tide is set": request.method == "made" or request.method == "arm" or request.method == "set" then delvetalk {request.object} haunt
body: inhabitant
